\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Output geometry suggests where dense preconditioning is worth its cost.} \textbf  {(a)} Diagonal and off-diagonal shares of anisotropy for all 11 moments (130M, Muon trajectory, step 2,500). Each bar shows the 32-layer median of $\mathrm  {DiagAniso}$ from \cref  {eq:diag_aniso} and its complement, $1-\mathrm  {DiagAniso}$. The split describes where anisotropy lies in the model's coordinate basis; it does not show its total magnitude. The cost column gives each moment's share of nominal dense eigendecomposition work across all 11 moments; teal marks the two moments WT-MLP-Lag diagonalizes. Expanded outputs have mostly diagonal anisotropy and account for 96.2\% of output-side cubic work; the equally wide \texttt  {down} input retains cross-channel structure. \textbf  {(b)} Final held-out and Paloma gains versus Muon at 520M, against median step-time overhead on 32 A100 GPUs. WT-MLP-Lag extends MuonT's quality gain with an incremental throughput cost. This run uses one seed.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Output geometry suggests where dense preconditioning is worth its cost.} \textbf {(a)} Diagonal and off-diagonal shares of anisotropy for all 11 moments (130M, Muon trajectory, step 2,500). Each bar shows the 32-layer median of $\mathrm {DiagAniso}$ from \cref {eq:diag_aniso} and its complement, $1-\mathrm {DiagAniso}$. The split describes where anisotropy lies in the model's coordinate basis; it does not show its total magnitude. The cost column gives each moment's share of nominal dense eigendecomposition work across all 11 moments; teal marks the two moments WT-MLP-Lag diagonalizes. Expanded outputs have mostly diagonal anisotropy and account for 96.2\% of output-side cubic work; the equally wide \texttt {down} input retains cross-channel structure. \textbf {(b)} Final held-out and Paloma gains versus Muon at 520M, against median step-time overhead on 32 A100 GPUs. WT-MLP-Lag extends MuonT's quality gain with an incremental throughput cost. This run uses one seed}{figure.caption.2}{}}
