\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Projection role separates the geometry across three optimizer trajectories.} \textbf  {(a)} Median diagonal share of anisotropy, $\mathrm  {DiagAniso}$ in \cref  {eq:diag_aniso}, across 32 layers at step 2,500 (130M); its complement is the off-diagonal share. Expanded outputs are mostly diagonal, while residual outputs \texttt  {o,down} carry less than 1\% of anisotropy on the diagonal. \textbf  {(b)} Mean top-16 eigenspace drift across 32 layers from steps 2,250 to 2,500, defined in \cref  {eq:subspace_drift} and derived in \cref  {app:diagnostic_definitions}; zero means identical subspaces and one means orthogonal subspaces. \textbf  {(c)} Cumulative exact-root fallbacks across eight GPUs in the dense-output diagnostic run. Outputs require frequent eigenbasis repairs; inputs require only 29 post-warmup fallbacks.}}{4}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
