\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Output-subspace drift with Muon as the baseline.} Fixed-data top-16 drift, averaged equally over 32 layers, two probe sets, and 19 intervals of 250 steps at 130M or three intervals of 2,560 steps at 520M. Seed-0 trajectories use learning rate 0.016 for Muon and 0.02263 for MuonT/WT; these compare the recorded training configurations and do not isolate optimizer effects at a common learning rate. Fresh 130M seeds 1--3 use 0.016 for all methods and one 2,560--5,120 interval each. Reductions are $100(1-\overline  D_{\rm  method}/\overline  D_{\rm  Muon})$; positive values mean lower drift than Muon. Seed summaries are mean $\pm $ sample SD across three seeds. The all-role row averages drift before taking ratios; absolute drift is not compared across model sizes. WT denotes WT-MLP-Lag.}}{19}{table.caption.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:output_drift}{{10}{19}{\textbf {Output-subspace drift with Muon as the baseline.} Fixed-data top-16 drift, averaged equally over 32 layers, two probe sets, and 19 intervals of 250 steps at 130M or three intervals of 2,560 steps at 520M. Seed-0 trajectories use learning rate 0.016 for Muon and 0.02263 for MuonT/WT; these compare the recorded training configurations and do not isolate optimizer effects at a common learning rate. Fresh 130M seeds 1--3 use 0.016 for all methods and one 2,560--5,120 interval each. Reductions are $100(1-\overline D_{\rm method}/\overline D_{\rm Muon})$; positive values mean lower drift than Muon. Seed summaries are mean $\pm $ sample SD across three seeds. The all-role row averages drift before taking ratios; absolute drift is not compared across model sizes. WT denotes WT-MLP-Lag}{table.caption.50}{}}
